Wait, but `npm start` calls `node api/server.js` which needs to start the server. If I remove the auto-start, `npm start` won't work either. I need a way to differentiate between:
1. Running as `node api/server.js` (production) → should start listening
2. Imported by test file → should NOT start listening

The simplest way: check if the module is the main module (not imported).

```js
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
// ...
if (process.argv[1] === new URL(import.meta.url).pathname) {
  app.listen(PORT, () => console.log(...));
}
```

Or more simply, use `require.main === module` equivalent in ESM. Actually in ESM, I can use `process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)`.

Or even simpler: just set `MODO_TESTE=1` when running tests, and keep the `if (MODO_TESTE !== '1')` condition.

Let me go back to the MODO_TESTE approach and just set it when running tests.

