Actually, the cleanest solution is to just change the server.js to check `process.argv[1]` to determine if it's the main module, rather than relying on `MODO_TESTE`. Or even simpler — just always start the server, and in the test file use a different port.

Wait, the real problem might be simpler: the server.js auto-starts at import time (because `MODO_TESTE` isn't set), and then the test tries to call `app.listen(0)` which fails because Express doesn't allow listening twice.

Let me fix this differently: instead of using `app.listen(0)` in the test, I'll check if the server is already listening and get the port from there. Or better yet, I'll restructure the server so that it never auto-starts and the test starts it explicitly.

